  "body": "## Current head `4727a4d7c` (2026-11-19 refresh)\n\nThe branch now carries the updated #2663 head (`3c89af10f`) and current `origin/main` (`971c23faa`). Hand-resolved conflicts and the gate results are in the last comment (class DELTA). #2663 must merge first; this PR then takes another `origin/main` refresh at merge time if needed.\n\n## Stacked on #2663  This branch is cut from #2663's head (`04ca39479`), because both change the tool pages. The base is `main`, so the file list below also shows #2663's files. Review the delta: commit `963d7c38` and commit `1fea5669`. See Issue Law \"Overlapping issues stack\": retarget this PR to `main` before #2663 merges, then merge #2663, then take `origin/main` here and gate again.  ## What changed  The tool body and profile editor gets its own window. Properties now holds only the tool's settings.  - `crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs` - new `tool_shape_editor_window` (`Tool shape: <name>`, 620x640, scrolling body, fixed `Close`). The old combined `tool_editor_window` is gone. - `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_settings.rs` - Properties shows the settings grid, one side preview, `Delete`, `Apply` / `Add tool`, and the `Edit tool shape` door. - `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_profile_page.rs` and `tool_cutter_page.rs` - two columns inside the window: controls left, points and side view right. The holder library comes first, then the Body / Profile tabs. The import and export row wraps. - `crates/ui/src/state.rs`, `actions.rs` - `State::tool_shape_editor`, `State::new_tool_form`, `open_tool_shape_editor`, `begin_new_tool`, `close_tool_shape_editor`. - `docs/decisions/2397-tool-shape-window.md` - the decision record.  `New toolΓÇª` opens the blank draft on Properties, not the shape window. A tool that does not exist yet has no shape. `Add tool` then `Edit tool shape` opens the window.  ## Pinning tests  - `properties_shows_the_settings_and_the_shape_window_holds_the_shape` - `the_holder_library_is_the_first_thing_the_shape_editor_shows` - `layout_window_tool_shape` (new), `layout_page_tool` - `tool_settings_edit_live_and_the_shape_editor_follows_its_tool` - `close_tool_shape_editor_keeps_the_tool` - `open_tool_shape_editor_syncs_the_draft_from_the_world` - `tool_editor_structure`, `tool_cutter_params_structure` - `the_tool_page_shows_one_preview_and_no_idle_3d_view`  The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes from 1379 on `main` to 1382 on this branch. No test was deleted or ignored. No snapshot PNG changed.  ## Gate on the final head `1fea5669`  - `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --test-threads=4`: 1220 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored (106 s). - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets`: 0 warnings, 0 errors. - The first full run had one red: `inch_mode_drag_keeps_px_parity_and_types_onto_the_lattice`. The settings moved down the Properties page, so `Apply` sits below the scroll fold at the default shell height and the bare click hit nothing. `1fea5669` adds the `scroll_to_me` idiom the op-page draft test already carries. No product change.  ## Maintainer GUI check  The maintainer ran this build on 2026-11-19 and reported it works. He also accepted the window title, the 620x640 size, the two-column split, and the `New toolΓÇª` door.  ## Not exercised  - The pixel snapshot `tool_editor_snapshot` stays `#[ignore]` in the release lane. Its golden shows the old layout and is regenerated at the cut. The structural twin is updated. - Real desktop window drag and resize: only the kittest layout is pinned. - The known Windows reds (CRLF goldens, stale `thread_boss` / `thread_mill` NC goldens, the wrapped 4-axis program test) were not run. - The four files this branch adds lines to are already past the 400-line guide on `main` (`pages.rs`, `actions.rs`, `state.rs`, `tests.rs`). This branch does not split them. A follow-up issue would help.  Changelog: Tool body and profile editing moved out of Properties into its own window, with the holder library and the Body / Profile tabs.  Fixes #2397 ",
